course: dictionary
lesson: 9919
title: Tan: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word tan can change meaning depending on the words around it. It can be a noun (a tan), a verb (to tan) or an adjective (tan shoes). The sentence tells you which meaning you need.
explain: «A tan is a sign the sun has already harmed the skin, not a shield, so tanned skin still needs sunscreen.» Here a tan is not something good to want. The sentence says the sun has damaged the skin, so the context shows the meaning is about harm, not beauty.
explain: Tan can also be a colour, as in «a tan dog» or tan shoes, which means light yellow-brown. In history, to tan leather means to turn animal skin into leather. Same word, different jobs, so always check the sentence.
fact: A tan is the brown colour skin gets after being in the sun.
fact: «Sunburn is a burn too, from invisible ultraviolet rays, and you can get it on a cloudy day.»
fact: A tan is not healthy skin; it is a sign that UV has damaged the skin.
fact: Tan as a colour means a light yellow-brown.
fact: In maths, tan is short for tangent, for older pupils.
exercise: «A tan is a sign the sun has already harmed the skin.» What does a tan show? | Skin that has been washed | *Skin that the sun has damaged | Skin that is cold | Skin that is healthy and strong
exercise: «Her new shoes were tan.» What colour are the shoes? | Bright red | Bright green | *Light yellow-brown | Bright blue
exercise: Sam says a tan means your skin is healthy. What is the best reply? | Sam is right, a tan is good for you | A tan means you have a new hat | *A tan shows UV has damaged the skin, so it is not healthy | A tan means you are cold
test: Which sentence uses tan as a verb? | The dog was tan | Put on your tan hat | *We will tan on the beach if we are careful | A tan is brown skin
test: Why do you still need sun cream on a cloudy day? | Sun cream is only for hot weather | Clouds make your skin stronger | Cloudy days have no sun at all | *Sunburn can happen on cloudy days from invisible UV rays
exam: What is the safest way to enjoy the sun? | Get a tan quickly before summer | *Wear sun cream, a hat and stay in the shade | Stay in the sun all day to get a tan | Put oil on your skin and lie down
